quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  21,58,Then Ibrahim (Abraham) broke those (idols) into pieces except the biggest (idol) so that they might turn to it.
  21,59,"They said: ‘Who has done this to our gods? Surely, he is of the wrongdoers.’"
  21,60,(Some of the) people said: ‘We have heard of a young man who speaks of them (with denial and disgust). He is known as Ibrahim (Abraham).’
  21,61,They said: ‘Bring him before the people so that they may see (him).’
  21,62,"(When Ibrahim [Abraham] came) they said: ‘O Ibrahim (Abraham), is it you who have done this to our gods?’"
  21,63,"He said: ‘Nay, this biggest (idol) of them would have done this. So ask these (very idols) if they can speak.’"
  21,64,"Then they turned to their own (reflections) and said: ‘Surely, you yourselves have become the wrongdoers (by worshipping these helpless idols incapable of doing anything).’"
  21,65,"Then they were turned upside down upon their heads (i.e., their thinking reverted and they said: ‘Ibrahim [Abraham]), surely you yourself know that they do not speak.’"
  21,66,"(Ibrahim [Abraham]) said: ‘Then do you worship apart from Allah these (idols) which can neither bring you any benefit, nor do you any harm?"
  21,67,Fie on you and (also) on these (idols) that you worship apart from Allah! Do you not then have sense?’
  21,68,They said: ‘Burn him and help your (ruined) gods if you have to do (something).’
  21,69,"We said: ‘O fire, be cool and become absolute safety for Ibrahim (Abraham).’"
  21,70,And they had intended an evil plot against Ibrahim (Abraham) but We failed them badly.
  21,71,"And (from Iraq) We rescued Ibrahim (Abraham) and Lut (Lot, his nephew, the son of his brother Haran,) towards (Syria), the land in which We have placed blessings for the people of the world."
  21,72,"And We blessed him with (a son) Ishaq (Isaac) and (by his prayer a grandson) Ya‘qub (Jacob) in addition, and We made all of them pious."
